Set in `.entire/settings.json` (or `settings.local.json` for personal-only):

```json
{
  "strategy_options": {
    "push_sessions": false
  }
}
```

Effect: checkpoints/transcripts stop pushing to remote on git push. Local capture (shadow refs) still happens — just nothing leaves your machine. Checked via `IsPushSessionsDisabled()` in `cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings.go:2105`.

Note: committed (non-local) settings affect everyone who clones the repo. Use `settings.local.json` if you want it personal-only.

